# Flow chart requirements

Follow these constraints on every change in this repository.

## Language and libraries

- JavaScript / ES6 and Vue 3 `<script setup>` only. Do not add TypeScript.
- Canvas rendering uses [Vue Flow](https://github.com/bcakmakoglu/vue-flow): `@vue-flow/core`, `@vue-flow/background`, `@vue-flow/controls`, `@vue-flow/minimap`. Do not replace `<VueFlow>` with a hand-rolled graph, and do not copy example source from that repository.
- Fetching and mutations use [TanStack Query v5](https://tanstack.com/query/v5) through `@tanstack/vue-query`. Do not use `@tanstack/react-query`, Vue Query v4, or `cacheTime`.
- Keep this query client config exact:

```js
queryClientConfig: {
  defaultOptions: {
    queries: {
      refetchOnWindowFocus: false,
      networkMode: 'always',
      staleTime: Infinity,
      gcTime: 60 * 60 * 1000,
    },
  },
}
```

- Pinia stores the graph, positions, selection, and undo history. Vue Router owns `/` and `/nodes/:nodeId`.

## Payload

- Preserve stored ids and `parentId` types. The trigger id is the number `1`. Other ids are strings. Compare with `String()` only at the Vue Flow boundary.
- Create-form values map as `sendMessage` → `sendMessage`, `addComments` → `addComment`, `businessHours` → `dateTime` with `data.action: "businessHours"` plus success and failure `dateTimeConnector` children.
- `dateTimeConnector` nodes are display-only. Do not open a drawer, do not select them as edit targets, and redirect direct visits to `/`.
- Do not delete the trigger. Deleting a node removes its subtree.
- Put shared helpers in `src/utils/`. Keep components free of layout math, id generation, and validation rules.

## UI and quality

- Every canvas node shows an icon, a title, and one truncated description.
- Validate title, description, comment, message text, attachment type and size, and business-hours ranges before writing them.
- Drawer open and close stays animated.
- Do not copy flowchart project source. Custom node components and CSS only.
- Add or update unit tests when logic or component behavior changes.
